# regatta crontab — operator copies the relevant lines into the host
# crontab via `crontab -e`. Each entry is opt-in; comment a line to
# disable that cadence.
#
# Format: m h dom mon dow  command
# All times UTC; flip TZ in /etc/crontab if local-time is preferred.

# Daily digest (PHASE-OBS): renders yesterday's UTC-day metrics file.
0 9 * * * /usr/local/bin/regatta-cron-daily-digest

# Self-improvement detector scan (PHASE-AUTONOMY W4): nightly rule
# sweep over the substrate. Default is dry-run (no --apply) so the
# first-deploy run never spam-files GH issues from a noisy ruleset
# (#646). Operator inspects one clean audit, then appends --apply to
# this line manually — per spec §8.1 amendment.
0 3 * * * /usr/local/bin/regatta self-improve scan
